-- title:
--   Special-fibre stalks of the X₁(Mp) two-chart model are valuation rings
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p)` $\subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with the tower $A \subseteq L \subseteq K$; let $j \in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Write $X$ for [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two morphisms of spectra induced by the inclusions of the chart algebras $B_{\mathrm{fin}} = \{x \in K : x \text{ integral over } A[j]\}$ and $B_{\infty} = \{x \in K : x \text{ integral over } A[j^{-1}]\}$ into the middle algebra, and `toBase` for its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $z \in X$, and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ through `toBase` (via the global-sections isomorphism for $\operatorname{Spec} A$); assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ and that $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} \mathcal{O}_{X,z} \le 1$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a valuation subring $V$ of $K$, a ring isomorphism $e \colon \mathcal{O}_{X,z} \simeq V$, and a witness that $z$ lies in the open image of the $j$-finite chart [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231), such that: $\operatorname{algebraMap} A K$ sends $A$ into $V$ and the maximal ideal of $A$ into the nonunits of $V$; for every $P \in A[T]$ whose reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ is nonzero, both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$; $e(\varpi_z) = \varpi$ in $K$; $e$ sends the germ at $z$ of the section coming from $a \in A$ to $a$; and for every $a \in B_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $e$ sends the germ at $z$, on the open image of the $j$-finite chart, of the section corresponding to $a$ to $a$ itself in $K$.
--
--   This identifies the local ring of the two-chart integral model of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring above $p$, at a point of the special fibre of Krull dimension at most one, with a valuation subring of the function field, and pins down how $A$, the uniformiser and the $j$-finite chart functions are read inside that valuation ring. It feeds the analysis of the special fibre of the model — the computation of its branch ideal and Krull dimension bounds, and the description of points and components of the fibre over $p$ — in the downstream study of $X_1(Mp)$ in mixed characteristic.
